I don't provide any image that because my images, don't respect default OpenWrt configuration, I have totally made my own thing, via the amazing OpenWrt SDK.
It's still an OpenWrt but it's ready out of the box for my own personal usage. Here is what I have done:

<code>
 Compile nativelly the entire GNU Core Utilities, and not install busybox
 Compile nativelly NTPD
 Compile nativelly SSHD and not install dropbear
 Compile nativelly Asterisk 11 - chan_sscp-b (for Cisco support)
 Compile nativelly DJBDNS and not dnsmasq then not install dhcp server thing
 Compile nativelly StrangSwan an IPSEC thing
 Not install Luci
 Inject all my default config file, via the ./script/env and ./file/ directory
</code>

